cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use jdx in research or writing, please cite it as below."
type: software
title: "jdx: an IDE for AI agents, as a command line tool"
abstract: >-
  jdx answers the questions an IDE answers for a human (members, method bodies,
  usages, type hierarchies, call graphs, public-API diffs) for AI coding agents,
  from JVM jars, sources jars, class and source directories, Maven coordinates
  and the JDK. It ships as a CLI and a Model Context Protocol (MCP) server.
authors:
